# ─── Nox PiDog Network Config ───
# Zentrale Netzwerk-Konfiguration fuer alle PiDog-Services.
# EDIT THIS FILE BEFORE STARTING THE SERVICES — the values below are examples.
# Bei IP-Aenderung nur DIESE Datei anpassen, dann:
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart nox-bridge nox-voice
#
# Brain = the machine running the brain (Pi 5, desktop, ...).
# Use its LAN or Tailscale IP; 127.0.0.1 only if brain and body
# run on the SAME machine (i.e. on the robot itself).
BRAIN_HOST=192.168.1.100
BRAIN_CALLBACK_PORT=8889
#
# Clawdbot Gateway (fuer Voice Loop v1 Fallback) — optional, same host as brain
CLAWDBOT_HOST=192.168.1.100
CLAWDBOT_PORT=18789
#
# ─── Autonomous behavior ───
# The bridge starts Nox's behavior engine at boot: the dog idles, patrols and
# plays on its own. Uncomment to disable it — the dog then only moves on your
# commands (it can still be started on demand: POST /behavior/start).
# The LEDs keep breathing either way: the daemon uses them as a status light.
# Apply with: sudo systemctl restart nox-bridge
#NOX_NO_AUTO=1
#
# ─── Audio output ───
# Unset (recommended): sound goes to the ALSA default, which SunFounder's own
# installer configures — on the PiDog that is the robot_hat speaker, which
# registers as a "Google voiceHAT" sound card.
# AUDIODEV=auto        → detect a speaker card, skipping HDMI outputs
# AUDIODEV=plughw:2,0  → pin one card; check the numbers with: aplay -l
# The daemon logs which device it uses and why, and refuses a card that does
# not exist instead of playing into the void.
#AUDIODEV=auto
